From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:45:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] config: add riscv64 to the Linux host-arch table

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; python-wheels does not open issues/PRs on third-party repos]

epicscorelibs.config._makeconf() maps platform.machine() to an EPICS
EPICS_HOST_ARCH-style label (linux-x86_64, linux-arm, linux-ppc,
linux-x86); any other value, including riscv64, falls through to
raise RuntimeError("Unsupported Linkage: " + machine). Nothing else
in this build (setuptools_dso's ProbeToolchain, the CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS
assembled in _makebuild(), the vendored EPICS libcom/ca/pvData/pvAccess
sources) branches on CPU architecture beyond this one table: atomics
go through GCC's __atomic/__sync builtins, byte order comes from
glibc's <sys/param.h>, and valgrind.h self-disables (defines
NVALGRIND) on any platform without one of its listed PLAT_* macros.
Add a linux-riscv64 label alongside the existing linux-arm/linux-ppc
entries so epicscorelibs.config.get_config_var('EPICS_HOST_ARCH')
resolves instead of raising.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/python/epicscorelibs/config.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/python/epicscorelibs/config.py b/src/python/epicscorelibs/config.py
index b9b0b945b..6919e9ba2 100644
--- a/src/python/epicscorelibs/config.py
+++ b/src/python/epicscorelibs/config.py
@@ -55,6 +55,8 @@ def _makeconf():
             HA = 'linux-ppc'
         elif machine.startswith('arm') or machine=="aarch64":
             HA = 'linux-arm'
+        elif machine=='riscv64':
+            HA = 'linux-riscv64'
         elif machine.endswith('86'):
             HA = 'linux-x86'
         else:
